prm-rtl8029.device history

0.19 (06.09.2001)

  FIXED: Interrupt server routine - should no more lock up with long
         files transferred by FTP.

  ADDED: AbortIO() proper handling.


0.20 (09.09.2001)

  ADDED: Raw packet support in CMD_WRITE and S2_BROADCAST (it was already done
         for CMD_READ).


0.21 (09.09.2001)

  ADDED: Support for PROMISCUOUS and EXCLUSIVE mode per unit.


0.22 (12.09.2001)

  FIXED: Bug in SendPacket() caused every not SANA2IOF_RAW packet had 14
         bytes of trash appended at the end.

  FIXED: Bug in InitUnit() - UnitData pointer was not initialized at
         first device opening.


0.23 (17.09.2001)

  ADDED: Support for S2_GETGLOBALSTATS command.

  FIXED: S2_ONLINE now returns error when called before
         S2_CONFIGINTERFACE.

  FIXED: Write and read queues are now flushed with S2ERR_OUTOFSERVICE
         on S2_OFFLINE command.

  FIXED: Write and read requests are rejected with S2ERR_OUTOFSERVICE if
         the device is in offline state.
	
      
1.0 (16.09.2002)

  ADDED: Support for PRM_BoardOwner tag of prometheus.library.
	
      
1.1 (04.10.2002)

  FIXED: S2_GETSTATIONADDRES returns MAC address from card ROM in
	 ios2_DstAddr, and address set by software in ios2_SrcAddr.
	 
  FIXED: S2_CONFIGINTERFACE allows for overriding hardware address.
  
  ADDED: S2_CONFIGINTERFACE rejects 00:00:00:00:00:00 and FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF
	 addresses.

  FIXED: Added calls to HardwareReset() and HardwareInit() fix the problem
	 with bad first read of hardware address after power on.

1.2 (06.10.2002)

  FIXED: Device was added to the system list even if opening of libraries
	 failed. It fixes hangups when trying to open the device with 1.x
	 prometheus.library (the device requires 2.x).
	 
1.3 (11.11.2002)

  FIXED: A loop in interrupt handler could be leaved in spite of pending
	 interrupts. It could lead to lost packets in heavy network traffic and
	 slow CPU.

2.0 (23.11.2026)

  Port to openpci.library by Steen Lund.

  CHANGED: Renamed to openpci-rtl8029.device. Uses openpci.library, so it
           works with any PCI bridge that library supports instead of only
           the Prometheus.

  FIXED: Full-size frames (1511 bytes and more) were dropped. The byte
         count in the receive ring includes 4 bytes beyond the frame,
         which were passed on and made full-size frames exceed the MTU.
         This stalled web browsing.

  FIXED: Receive ring boundary handling and the byte order of the receive
         packet header. A corrupt ring header is detected and the ring
         reset.

  CHANGED: The interrupt server only masks the card's interrupts and
           signals the unit task; all card access happens in the unit
           task. No more Disable()/Enable(): the request queues are
           protected by semaphores.

  CHANGED: S2_ONLINE, S2_OFFLINE and S2_CONFIGINTERFACE run in the unit
           task. Going offline returns all pending requests with
           S2ERR_OUTOFSERVICE.

  FIXED: Closing the device from another task than the one that opened
         it hung (Roadshow's NetShutdown). Unit expunge fixed, and
         exclusive opens are enforced.

  FIXED: Write requests are validated and frames carry the station
         address set with S2_CONFIGINTERFACE.

  ADDED: Recovery from a full receive ring that keeps the frames already
         in it. The card is stopped for less than 2 ms.

  CHANGED: Faster: packet data moves through the card 32 bits at a time,
           the card has two transmit buffers so the next frame is
           uploaded while one is sent, read and write requests are queued
           without a task switch, and frames are longword aligned for the
           TCP/IP stack. FTP transfers ran at about 505 KB/s before; a
           TCP benchmark now reaches about 750 KB/s receiving and 950 KB/s
           sending on the same machine.

  ADDED: Checks with mmu.library whether the card's registers are mapped
         cache-inhibited and flushes the caches around accesses if not.

  ADDED: Diagnostic counters through S2_GETSPECIALSTATS, including the
         card's own error tallies, collisions and the unit task's state.
         The s2stat tool prints them, grouped by topic.

  ADDED: The unit task priority (default 6) can be set without
         rebuilding: SetEnv openpci-rtl8029.pri <n>.

  ADDED: Unsupported SANA-II commands are answered with
         S2ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED.

  FIXED: Running the device from a Shell returns harmlessly, the ROMTag
         reports version 2, and a failed initialisation (for example
         without openpci.library) no longer leaks memory.

  CHANGED: The installer works with openpci: it finds the card with lspci
           from the openpci package, shows its progress, and asks before
           reinstalling the same version.

  ADDED: openpci-rtl8029.guide, an AmigaGuide covering installation, the
         task priority setting, the test client and every s2stat counter.
